  "rationale": "The provided typed ODE contract is preserved exactly as required: this is a coupled ODE system in time with target state C, and the scored expression is the C-component of that system. The chosen rates keep all hazards positive and on 0-30 day scales that visibly resolve the recorded mechanisms without collapsing to the parent-recovery limits. progression_rate=0.35 moves the initial latent cohort out of L over a few time units, but because M(0)=P(0)=C(0)=0 the inherited serial chain still enforces the intended delayed buildup of C rather than immediate growth. presymptomatic_progression_rate=0.7 makes the added P stage finite but not negligible, so the generation-4 delay/filtering remains visible instead of becoming quasi-instantaneous. clearance_rate=0.2 gives an infectious removal timescale comparable to, but slower than, the P-to-C progression timescale, allowing a clear rise, peak, and decay within t in [0,30]. maturation_heterogeneity=0.01 is strong enough to bend the M-to-P transfer away from a single linear gain over reachable M values (tens to low hundreds) but not so strong that the transfer is saturated for most of the trajectory. contagious_feedback=0.01 provides moderate suppression when C reaches moderate levels, flattening and delaying inflow during high-C phases while leaving early low-C behavior close to the simpler law; this exposes the generation-3 interaction without dominating all dynamics. The suggested bound for contagious_clearance_burden is respected with value 0.03, which makes burden-accelerated clearance negligible near C≈0 yet visibly stronger around moderate/high C, exposing the generation-5 extra downward curvature and sharper post-peak decay. The inherited initial state means the added-stage mechanisms are activated naturally by trajectory evolution, not by altering initial conditions. Weak/inactive limits are avoided: none of maturation_heterogeneity, contagious_feedback, or contagious_clearance_burden is set near zero, but none is pushed so high that denominators become dominated by saturation over the full run. Exact noiseless trajectories should therefore show delayed emergence of C from the latent chain, later and flatter peak timing than simpler parent laws, and faster decline once contagious burden becomes substantial.",
